# Blade Template Conventions

## Slug-based page routing

Content pages map to WordPress Pages by slug — there is no catch-all template:

| Template file | Required WP page slug |
|---|---|
| `front-page.blade.php` | (site front page) |
| `page-tours.blade.php` | `tours` |
| `page-guides.blade.php` | `guides` |
| `page-area.blade.php` | `area` |
| `page-contact.blade.php` | `contact` |

Editing a `page-{slug}.blade.php` only takes effect if a published Page with that exact slug exists (created by `bin/setup-wp.sh`).

## Layout and shared partials

- All pages extend `layouts.app`
- Shared sections: `partials/info-strip`, `partials/book-band`
- Shop URL: use `wc_get_page_permalink('shop')` with `home_url('/shop')` fallback

```blade
@php
  $shopUrl = function_exists('wc_get_page_permalink') ? wc_get_page_permalink('shop') : home_url('/shop');
@endphp
```

## After editing Blade files — clear Acorn cache

Blade templates are compiled and cached by Acorn. Changes won't appear until the cache is cleared:

```bash
wp acorn view:clear --path="$HOME/wp" --allow-root
# or
wp acorn optimize:clear --path="$HOME/wp" --allow-root
```

## After editing CSS/JS — rebuild Vite assets

```bash
npm run build
```

Pages throw a fatal "Vite manifest not found" error if `public/build/` is missing.
